-- name    : CountingMatroid_Analysis_FiniteTapePhaseControl
-- status  : Definition
-- author  : @marwahaha
-- created : 2026-10-24T14:50:49.703588+00:00
-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/d90aca75-0622-4b2b-a80c-e651aec51ab3
-- title:
--   An accurate phase-ratio factorization of the actual run output
-- statement:
--   Fix natural parameters $n,r$, independence oracles $o_1,o_2$, rational accuracy and confidence inputs $0<\varepsilon,\delta<1$, and a Boolean tape $b:\mathbb N\to\{0,1\}$. Let $s$ be the resulting setup schedule, with cooling factor $\rho$, relative-error parameter $\eta$, and phase count $L$. Write $C_j$ for the operational transversal partition sum at parameter $\rho^j$, namely the sum of $\rho^{j d(A)}$ over subsets $A\subseteq[n]$, where $d(A)$ is the operational deficiency of the corresponding transversal.
--
--   The predicate $\operatorname{AccurateRatioProduct}$ asserts the existence of rational ratios $R_j$ such that the actual numerical single-run output $Y$ satisfies
--   $$Y=2^n\prod_{j=0}^{L-1}R_j,$$
--   and, for every $j<L$,
--   $$\frac{1-\eta}{1+\eta}\leq
--   \frac{R_j}{C_{j+1}/C_j}
--   \leq\frac{1+\eta}{1-\eta}.$$
--   This is a deterministic certificate for the numerical output and its factorization. The definition does not separately require a successful optional execution witness or assert a probability bound. Quotients use the rational field's total division convention.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/FiniteTapePhaseControl.lean#L23-L37

